From 1515ba59579f750790e09de0023057ade23d8594 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:45:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): judge a picked Circular against its part; Slot
 shares authored_law

A Circular whose source is a pick of the finished part took
DepthLaw::None, so a ring typed below its picked floor read clean on the
operation; with a rotated stock the program sim refuses to judge and
uncovered() accepts that empty verdict, so the overcut could post.
authored_law now judges picks too (Entity | Selection -> Section, Stock
-> None), and the Slot arm calls it as well, so the one shared law is
real code. The Slot's law is unchanged (Section for every part-solid
source since #1504 / #1537; part_solid is never true for Stock).

Pins: circular_pick_law (picked ring 3 mm below its floor with a rotated
stock: op gouges, post refused by name on the op's moves; MCP verify
names the op's gouge; at the floor clean; a pick off a from-model stock
never judged - the part_solid early return's placement), and
authored_law_tests (picks Section, Slot through the same law). Decision
file: chord-sag readings corrected (64 chords refused at leave 0), why
Contain is not pinnable by integration for a Circular.

Fixes #1550
Refs #1543

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
